# Azure VM Deployment & Optimization Plan

We will optimize the codebase to handle large SQL dumps (2GB+) to prevent server crashes and set up a CI/CD pipeline for your Azure Virtual Machine.

## User Review Required

> [!CAUTION]
> **Memory Usage Warning**: The current code reads the entire SQL file into memory. A 2GB file will crash a small VM. I will fix this to stream the file or use system tools for the import.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Strategy**: For 2GB+ datasets, I **strongly recommend a separate database** (Azure Database for PostgreSQL or Supabase). 
> - **Pros**: Higher stability, easier scaling, won't crash your API server during heavy imports.
> - **Cons**: Additional cost.
>
> If you choose to keep the database on the VM, we need at least **8GB of RAM** and an **SSD**.

## Proposed Changes

### Core Optimization

#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- Refactor the `restore` logic to stop reading the whole file into memory.
- Use `subprocess` to call `psql` directly if possible, or stream the SQL in chunks.

### CI/CD Implementation

#### [NEW] [deploy.yml](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/.github/workflows/deploy.yml)
- Create a GitHub Actions workflow to:
  1. Build Docker images for `api`, `web`, and `worker`.
  2. Push images to **Docker Hub** (easiest for VM deployment).
  3. SSH into the Azure VM to pull the new images and restart the containers.

